{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>The well, which the princes dug.</b> That is, this well is not like other wells, which are dug by servants, as it says ״ויכרו שם עבדי יצחק באר״ — but this well is distinguished, that the princes dug it, and the nobles of the people carved it — Moses, Aaron, and the elders of Israel." "<b>With a staff, with their supports.</b> That is, they did not dig it like other wells, but carved it into the rock with the staff of Elohim. And this proves that the Holy One, blessed be He, did not take offense at his having struck it, for if He had taken offense, they would not have sung of a matter over which He took offense. And some explain: 'מחוקק' — this is Moses, as it says ״כי שם חלקת מחוקק ספון״, and we translate: Moses the great scribe." "<b>And from the wilderness, a gift. That is,</b> there was great importance in that well, for from the wilderness, which is a place of thirst, it was for them a source of water."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:47.724171849Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}